rain-core: xray/0055-muxcool-xray-interop
Source: ReClash test on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

Add a real Xray-core interop test, gated by MIHOMO_XRAY_BIN. It starts a
pinned Xray VLESS inbound (plain, TLS 1.3 and Vision) with a freedom outbound
that allows loopback for the harness, local TCP/UDP echo services, and drives
them through the mihomo mux.cool outbound: TCP, server-first, XUDP, concurrent
TCP+UDP, carrier rotation, TLS, Vision with UDP-only mux, XUDP GlobalID
rebind, and an Xray client with mux as the reference implementation. The
series repository runs it in CI with tool/xray_interop.sh, which downloads
Xray 26.11.9 and verifies its SHA256 before use.

Tests: TestXrayInterop (subtests TCP, ServerFirst, UDP, ConcurrentTCPAndUDP,
CarrierRotation, TLS, VisionXUDPOnly, XUDPGlobalIDRebind, ReferenceXrayClient).
